WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.280
Part 2. You will hear a talk to members of the public about plans for a new housing development

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:14.960
near a town called Nunston. First, you have some time to look at questions 11 to 14.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:39.279
Now listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 14.

00:00:42.959 --> 00:00:48.320
Hello everyone. It's good to see that so many members of the public have shown up for our

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:55.279
presentation on the new housing development planned on the outskirts of Nunston. I'm Mark

00:00:55.279 --> 00:01:02.720
Reynolds and I'm Communications Manager at the development. I'll start by giving you a brief

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:10.720
overview of our plans for the development. So, one thing I'm sure you'll want to know is why

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:18.400
we've selected this particular site for a housing development. At present, it's being used for

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:26.080
farming, like much of the land around Nunston. But because of the new industrial centre in

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:33.360
Nunston, there's a lot of demand for housing for employees in the region, as many employees

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:40.080
are having to commute long distances at present. Of course, there's also the fact that we have

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:48.160
an international airport just 20 minutes drive away. But, although that's certainly convenient,

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:55.839
it wasn't one of our major criteria for choosing the site. We were more interested in the fact that

00:01:55.839 --> 00:02:03.519
there's an excellent hospital just 15 kilometres away, and a large secondary school even closer

00:02:03.519 --> 00:02:13.679
than that. One drawback to the site is that it's on quite a steep slope, but we've taken account

00:02:13.679 --> 00:02:21.360
of that in our planning, so it shouldn't be a major problem. We've had a lot of positive feedback

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:29.679
about the plans. People like the wide variety of accommodation types and prices, and the fact that

00:02:29.679 --> 00:02:36.320
it's only a short drive to get out into the countryside from the development. We were

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:42.880
particularly pleased that so many people liked the designs for the layout of the development,

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:49.919
with the majority of people saying it generally made a good impression and blended in well with

00:02:49.919 --> 00:02:56.800
the natural features of the landscape, with provision made for protecting trees and wildlife

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:03.839
on the site. Some people have mentioned that they'd like to see more facilities for cyclists,

00:03:04.479 --> 00:03:10.960
and we'll look at that, but the overall feedback has been that the design and facilities of the

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:17.199
development make it seem a place where people of all ages can live together happily.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:26.720
Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 15 to 20.

00:03:41.919 --> 00:03:42.000
you

00:04:01.839 --> 00:04:05.520
Now listen and answer questions 15 to 20.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:15.600
OK, so I'll put a map of the proposed development up on the screen.

00:04:17.839 --> 00:04:24.559
You'll see it's bounded on the south side by the main road, which then goes on to Nunston.

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:31.119
Another boundary is formed by London Road on the western side of the development.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:38.399
Inside the development, there'll be about 400 houses and three apartment blocks.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:44.239
There'll also be a school for children up to 11 years old.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:52.000
If you look at the south entrance at the bottom of the map, there's a road from there that goes

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:58.880
right up through the development. The school will be on that road, at the corner of the second

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:08.000
turning to the left. A large sports centre is planned with facilities for indoor and outdoor

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:15.679
activities. This will be on the western side of the development, just below the road that branches

00:05:15.679 --> 00:05:23.839
off from London Road. There'll be a clinic where residents can go if they have any health problems.

00:05:24.799 --> 00:05:31.600
Can you see the lake towards the top of the map? The clinic will be just below this,

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:39.359
to the right of a street of houses. There'll also be a community centre for people of all ages.

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:46.640
On the northeast side of the development, there'll be a row of specially designed houses,

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:53.760
specifically for residents over 65, and the community centre will be adjoining this.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:06:02.079
We haven't forgotten about shopping. There'll be a supermarket between the two entrances to

00:06:02.079 --> 00:06:08.720
the development. We're planning to leave the three large trees near London Road,

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:16.480
and it'll be just to the south of these. It's planned to have a playground for younger children.

00:06:17.279 --> 00:06:23.440
If you look at the road that goes up from the south entrance, you'll see it curves round to

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:31.519
the left at the top, and the playground will be in that curve, with nice views of the lake.

00:06:32.559 --> 00:06:37.519
Okay, so, now, does anyone have any questions?

00:06:37.519 --> 00:06:46.399
That is the end of part two. You now have 30 seconds to check your answers to part two.

00:07:07.519 --> 00:07:08.019
Thank you.

